window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Marked by Death. Saved by a Vow.</b></p> <p>Katrin thought little of the dusky shadows when they first appeared on her fingertips. Nearly eight years later, those shadows cover half her body, along with a sprawling, ancient script that spells her doom.</p> <p>Ostracized, Kat has no choice but to hide away and watch life go on without her. She tries everything to remove her mark, but time is running out. Her only chance of survival lies with the one creature who might keep her from Death’s clutches—<i>The Ferrier of Souls.</i></p> <p>Straddling the worlds of the living and the dead, The Ferrier reluctantly agrees to harbor Katrin for one year—long enough to avoid her fated passing. But The Ferrier does nothing for free, and Kat may be in for more than she bargained for. With complicated feelings stirring between them, Kat finds herself dreading the day she returns to the world of the living.</p> <p>But she can't stay with the Ferrier forever…</p> <p><b>Fans of Belladonna and A Deal with the Elf King will fall in love with this atmospheric and enchanting fantasy romance inspired by Welsh mythology.</b></p>"; 
